        "mark_note": "Plan",
        "lines": [
          "Paramecium is a slipper-shaped single-celled",
          "organism with a blunt anterior end and a",
          "pointed posterior end.",
          "The body is covered by a pellicle and cilia",
          "are present all over it.",
          "The drawing must show the oral groove leading",
          "to the cytostome and cytopharynx, the two",
          "nuclei, the food vacuoles, the two contractile",
          "vacuoles and the cytopyge."
        ],
        "why": "Naming the shape and the parts before drawing fixes the order of work: the outline and cilia first, then the feeding path, then the contents.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing an oval cell. The slipper shape is asked for by name in most papers.",
          "Drawing cilia on one side only. They cover the whole body."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Blunt in front, pointed behind, and one groove cut into one side: that is the slipper shape.",
        "margin_note": "Three lines of plan. Do not describe fission or conjugation here."
