        "why": "The feeding path is drawn as one continuous line from the oral groove to the cytopyge, so the food vacuoles can be placed along it instead of scattered at random.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing one nucleus. Show the large macronucleus AND the small micronucleus beside it.",
          "Placing both contractile vacuoles together. One lies near the anterior end and one near the posterior end.",
          "Leaving out the cytopyge. It is the fixed opening near the posterior end where waste leaves."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Draw the slipper, then the cilia, then the groove and gullet, then the two nuclei, then the vacuoles, then label.",
        "margin_note": "Two marks sit here. The two nuclei and the two contractile vacuoles decide them."
