        "lines": [
          {
            "text": "2 nuclei, 2 contractile vacuoles, 1 gullet",
            "style": "boxed"
          },
          "The oral groove runs backwards along one side",
          "and ends at the cytostome.",
          "The cytostome opens into the cytopharynx,",
          "where food vacuoles are formed.",
          "The macronucleus is large and controls the",
          "everyday work of the cell. The micronucleus",
          "is small and takes part in reproduction.",
          "The two contractile vacuoles remove excess",
          "water, one at each end of the body.",
          "Undigested matter leaves through the",
          "cytopyge near the posterior end."
        ],
        "why": "Paramecium has a fixed mouth and a fixed anal spot, unlike Amoeba, so the labels are easiest to hold as one path: groove, cytostome, cytopharynx, food vacuole, cytopyge.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Swapping the two nuclei. The macronucleus is the large one and it is not the reproductive nucleus.",
          "Calling the cytopyge a mouth. It is the fixed opening for waste."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Follow the food: groove, cytostome, cytopharynx, food vacuole, cytopyge. That is five labels in one line of thought.",
